      "issue": "The fixture's own CLI entry never passes a roles file, so its temp-HOME ('none') runs of review.mjs still stop with no reviewer role. With no roles.json, lib/roles.js leaves the reviewer role unset, `model-id --role reviewer --json` exits 2, and review.mjs's poolOrStop exits 1. The CLI therefore reports all three none/review.mjs scenarios as FAILED and exits 1. The branch fixed this for tests/models-scripts.mjs only, by adding the `rolesFile` option, which the CLI has no flag for. Derived from reading the code; not run.",
      "file": "tests/fixtures/model-registry/inspect-scripts.mjs",
      "line": "154",
      "quote": "  const res = inspect({ homeFile: hf === -1 ? null : process.argv[hf + 1] });",
      "suggestion": "Add a `--roles-file <roles.json>` flag to the CLI entry and pass it through as `rolesFile` (or write a default reviewer role into the temp HOME when none is given), and name the flag in the header usage line.",
